    "body": "What terminal are you using? I used your _Starship_ configuration on _macOS_ with _iTerm_ and _Fish Shell_ and got the following (without the need to use <kbd>CTRL + c</kbd>):\r\n<img width=\"834\" alt=\"Starship-test\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/2911922/220111033-80f29677-70bc-4fe4-8652-e03314f3623c.png\">\r\nBesides, there is an error in your configuration:\r\n```bash\r\n[WARN] - (starship::config): Error in 'Battery' at 'display': Error in 'BatteryDisplay' at 'add_newline': Unknown key\r\n[WARN] - (starship::config): Failed to load config value: Error in 'Battery' at 'display': Error in 'BatteryDisplay' at 'add_newline': Unknown key\r\n```\r\nThe section with `add_newline = true` has to be directly below the format section, before any of the `[module]` sections.",
