    "updated_at": "2023-02-20T18:02:06Z",
    "body": "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n> What terminal are you using? I used your _Starship_ configuration on _macOS_ with _iTerm_ and _Fish Shell_ and got the following (without the need to use CTRL + c): <img alt=\"Starship-test\" width=\"834\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/2911922/220111033-80f29677-70bc-4fe4-8652-e03314f3623c.png\"> Besides, there is an error in your configuration:\r\n> \r\n> ```shell\r\n> [WARN] - (starship::config): Error in 'Battery' at 'display': Error in 'BatteryDisplay' at 'add_newline': Unknown key\r\n> [WARN] - (starship::config): Failed to load config value: Error in 'Battery' at 'display': Error in 'BatteryDisplay' at 'add_newline': Unknown key\r\n> ```\r\n> \r\n> The section with `add_newline = true` has to be directly below the format section, before any of the `[module]` sections.\r\n\r\nI am on Kitty Terminal. I just fixed the config issues you pointed out, but the issue seems to persist. It's hard to reproduce as it takes a few commands (none specific) before it starts acting this way. I was using the same config on my WSL2 setup, and had the same freezing. So it wasn't isolated to one device. Will reply with any other info I can find about possible causes.",
